=== non-KMS and not even single-copy passive (population inversion across modes) ===

T1=1.0, T2=3.0: w = [1.0, 2.0], T = [1.0, 3.0], beta_i*w_i = [1.0, 0.6667]
   single-copy ergotropy W_1 = 7.030e-02  -> NOT passive
   W_N / N, N = 1..: 7.030e-02 7.030e-02 7.030e-02 7.030e-02 7.052e-02 7.076e-02 7.109e-02 7.140e-02 7.164e-02
   asymptotic per-copy limit E - E(gibbs at equal entropy) = 7.4820e-02  (beta* = 0.5426)

=== single-copy passivity condition (two qubits): passive iff w1/T1 <= w2/T2 for w1<w2 ===
   2000 random cases agree with the analytic condition: True
   => for TWO modes single-copy passivity leaves a profile freedom (w/T(w) non-decreasing);
      the three-mode case above already fails: level w1+w2=1.5 < w3=1.7 but carries less population

=== many modes, ONE copy: how much temperature-profile freedom survives single-copy passivity? ===
   profile T(w) = T0*(1 + eps*(w-1)), T0 = 0.5, modes equally spaced in [0.5, 1.5]
   m= 2: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 1.0000 (eps>0 side)
   m= 3: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 1.0000 (eps>0 side)
   m= 4: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.1501 (eps>0 side)
   m= 6: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.0769 (eps>0 side)
   m= 8: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.0522 (eps>0 side)
   m=12: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.0151 (eps>0 side)
   m=16: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.0101 (eps>0 side)
   m=20: single-copy passive iff |eps| <~ 0.0073 (eps>0 side)
   dense-spectrum argument: levels {a,b} vs {c} with c ~ a+b force f(a)+f(b) = f(a+b), f(w) = w/T(w)
   (Cauchy) => f linear => single beta. A macroscopic bath acts as its own copies.

=== what complete passivity leaves: the FDT ratio shape fixed, its scale T free ===
   T=  0.1: noise/dissipation ratio coth(w/2T) at w=0.5,1,2 -> [1.0136 1.0001 1.    ]  ; in scaled variable w/T it is the same function
   T=  1.0: noise/dissipation ratio coth(w/2T) at w=0.5,1,2 -> [4.083 2.164 1.313]  ; in scaled variable w/T it is the same function
   T= 10.0: noise/dissipation ratio coth(w/2T) at w=0.5,1,2 -> [40.0083 20.0167 10.0333]  ; in scaled variable w/T it is the same function
